WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.190
Special Article: The Truth about Stepping Man

00:00.890 --> 00:05.480
The mysterious phantom Stepping Man?

00:01.770 --> 00:05.480
STEPPING

00:05.480 --> 00:09.310
A terrifying phantom that kidnaps
children under the cover of night!

00:09.310 --> 00:13.750
It can hop around in mid-air,
and no one in Labyrinth City can stop it!

00:13.750 --> 00:16.430
Don't you think that's romantic?

00:17.470 --> 00:19.980
"Romance" is one of those words
with a lot of definitions.

00:20.600 --> 00:23.040
If it's a bad person, we need to beat it.

00:23.040 --> 00:24.620
Don't waste your time on it.

00:24.620 --> 00:26.730
You know there's no such thing.

00:26.730 --> 00:29.760
Hey! Stepping Man is real!

00:29.760 --> 00:32.120
There are witnesses!

00:32.120 --> 00:35.510
Don't believe everything you read
in a cheap gossip rag like that.

00:35.510 --> 00:38.240
I'd love to meet Stepping Man.

00:39.090 --> 00:41.480
Did you just say, "Stepping Man"?

00:41.780 --> 00:46.550
I'm Olivia Taylor, an adventurer and
writer for <i>Lemuria Monthly</i> magazine!

00:46.550 --> 00:49.680
<i>Lemuria Monthly</i>? I love your magazine!

00:49.680 --> 00:51.980
Your words honor me.

00:51.980 --> 00:54.130
You just found out about it a while ago.

00:54.700 --> 00:57.500
That's a terrible thing
for an idol otaku to say.

00:57.500 --> 01:00.320
What does time have to do with love?

01:01.410 --> 01:04.560
You're no fun.

01:04.560 --> 01:08.090
Kizuna's curiosity is an
inspiration to us all.

01:08.090 --> 01:09.230
Kizuna?

01:15.530 --> 01:17.420
That's a wonderful name!

01:18.080 --> 01:20.250
Writer and adventurer?

01:20.990 --> 01:23.650
Yes, I may not look it,
but I'm an adventurer!

01:23.650 --> 01:27.850
So... I'm... actually...

01:27.850 --> 01:28.660
Yuck!

01:28.660 --> 01:32.020
Hop! Hop! Achoo!

01:33.570 --> 01:36.460
Thank you.

01:36.460 --> 01:38.490
Why are you moving around like that?

01:42.820 --> 01:46.230
Whenever there's something weird
going on in Labyrinth City,

01:46.230 --> 01:48.510
I'm always there to check it out.

01:51.000 --> 02:02.810
Ningen Fushin: Adventurers Who Don't
Believe in Humanity Will Save the World

03:21.510 --> 03:26.430
"The Legend of the Labyrinth City - Stepping Man?!"

03:45.580 --> 03:48.240
Well? How'd you enjoy your first concert?

03:48.240 --> 03:50.900
It was more fun than I thought it would be.

03:50.900 --> 03:53.840
Especially your favorite, Agate...

03:53.840 --> 03:56.000
Oh, you get it, huh?

03:56.000 --> 04:00.250
Indeed! I feel a strong light in her soul.

04:00.250 --> 04:02.810
In another era, she would
have been a shaman...

04:03.760 --> 04:04.640
What?

04:05.160 --> 04:06.510
Zem's in danger!

04:07.900 --> 04:09.120
Here!

04:09.920 --> 04:10.820
Zem!

04:14.570 --> 04:16.240
Stepping Man...

04:16.240 --> 04:18.360
A cheap conjurer's trick.

04:19.360 --> 04:23.050
How can we fight him when we can't see him?

04:24.530 --> 04:25.620
There!

04:28.490 --> 04:30.600
You can see me?

04:31.240 --> 04:32.780
I'm not done yet!

04:32.780 --> 04:34.830
Take this! Parallel!

04:34.830 --> 04:35.860
What?

04:43.920 --> 04:45.270
How boring.

04:49.940 --> 04:52.650
Can you wipe your face off?

04:56.940 --> 04:59.410
Thanks so much, Red.

04:59.410 --> 05:01.190
You owe me for this, Zem.

05:01.490 --> 05:03.620
We're not a hospital, you know.

05:03.620 --> 05:06.600
What were you doing out there that late?

05:06.600 --> 05:08.310
Any idea who that guy was?

05:09.100 --> 05:11.460
She just went through
something really scary.

05:11.460 --> 05:13.270
You don't have to interrogate her.

05:13.270 --> 05:14.600
S-Sorry.

05:17.490 --> 05:21.780
That's... Stepping Man!

05:22.940 --> 05:24.980
My mom's no liar!

05:24.980 --> 05:26.920
She's not...

05:32.710 --> 05:34.630
Tell me more.

05:36.490 --> 05:42.480
Mom would always go out late at night
to try and defeat Stepping Man.

05:42.480 --> 05:46.970
But she lost, and now she's in the hospital.

05:47.450 --> 05:48.610
Oh, my...

05:48.610 --> 05:51.080
My mom realized

05:51.080 --> 05:56.240
that all the disappearing children
lately were because of Stepping Man.

05:57.070 --> 06:00.960
But nobody would believe her...

06:01.570 --> 06:04.910
Well, most people wouldn't believe.

06:06.990 --> 06:10.020
But we saw it with our own eyes.

06:11.740 --> 06:15.200
We saw someone hiding themselves
in the darkness, attacking a child,

06:15.200 --> 06:19.200
and jumping from roof to roof with ease.

06:20.500 --> 06:23.140
Um, what's your name?

06:23.140 --> 06:24.280
Reina.

06:24.630 --> 06:28.540
Reina, we believe your mom.

06:29.140 --> 06:34.760
And I respect her bravery in challenging
such a difficult opponent all by herself.

06:35.250 --> 06:36.440
Zem...

06:37.900 --> 06:39.030
Zem!

06:40.030 --> 06:42.190
Please make me your student!

06:46.640 --> 06:49.060
My student?

06:49.060 --> 06:49.920
Yes.

06:49.920 --> 06:53.570
I was so impressed by how
brave you were back there!

06:54.460 --> 06:56.850
Listen, he was once...

06:56.850 --> 06:57.820
You're ten years...

06:59.620 --> 07:03.490
no, fifteen years too
young to be my student.

07:06.850 --> 07:08.200
Fifteen years?

07:10.940 --> 07:14.450
S-So how should I train until then?

07:14.450 --> 07:20.110
Well, for today, get some
rest at Miss Red's place.

07:20.110 --> 07:23.270
We can go see your mom in the morning.

07:23.270 --> 07:26.880
And never do anything so dangerous again.

07:28.210 --> 07:30.120
Okay, Master!

07:30.620 --> 07:36.180
Until fifteen years have passed,
you must not get any closer to me.

07:36.180 --> 07:37.250
Can you do that?

07:37.250 --> 07:38.480
I can!

07:38.710 --> 07:39.870
Good girl.

07:41.700 --> 07:42.750
This sucks.

07:43.710 --> 07:46.990
Oh, my... You're such a young boy to
be letting out such a big sigh...

07:47.250 --> 07:51.670
My beloved Stepping Man turned
out to be that cheap fraud.

07:52.210 --> 07:55.100
We got closer to finding out his
true identity. That's a big step.

07:55.870 --> 08:00.250
He doesn't have a "true identity".
He's just some kidnapper.

08:00.640 --> 08:03.730
I'm just going to have to destroy
this fake Stepping Man!

08:03.730 --> 08:05.750
I'll catch him myself!

08:05.750 --> 08:10.280
We can't leave him on the loose
after he hurt Reina, either.

08:11.680 --> 08:12.780
Then...

08:13.870 --> 08:15.740
Let's make a job out of it.

08:20.090 --> 08:25.970
This guild is filled with bounty hunters,
so it's a little rougher than most.

08:29.400 --> 08:31.730
Give us what you know about Stepping Man.

08:32.790 --> 08:35.680
I don't think I've seen
the four of them before.

08:35.680 --> 08:37.370
Oh, right.

08:37.370 --> 08:39.750
We can't share info on expensive bounties

08:39.750 --> 08:42.980
with adventurers who've never
accomplished anything.

08:42.980 --> 08:45.580
Mr. Former-Member-of-Masters-of-War.

08:48.260 --> 08:51.430
You just said the word
"expensive," didn't you?

08:51.430 --> 08:52.630
Bingo.

08:52.900 --> 08:55.020
So there is a bounty out on him.

08:55.020 --> 08:57.260
I didn't say that...

08:59.580 --> 09:01.630
Okay, how's this for starters?

09:02.050 --> 09:03.880
Hale Hardy...

09:03.880 --> 09:05.960
The reward is 300,000 dinah.

09:05.960 --> 09:07.390
That's not bad.

09:07.620 --> 09:10.100
You got the Iron Tigers sent to jail.

09:10.100 --> 09:13.170
This should be easy for you Survivors.

09:14.280 --> 09:15.530
Those are the Survivors?

09:15.530 --> 09:16.720
Wow!

09:16.720 --> 09:20.780
They ain't bounty hunters.
They're muscling in on our turf.

09:20.780 --> 09:23.810
Jealousy is unbecoming of a bounty hunter.

09:23.810 --> 09:27.220
You amateurs should stick
to fighting goblins!

09:27.220 --> 09:27.930
Stop it!

09:28.330 --> 09:29.430
Don't try to stop me!

09:29.430 --> 09:30.870
He doesn't mean anything by it!

09:30.870 --> 09:32.460
Please don't provoke him...

09:33.740 --> 09:37.740
We'll find this Hale guy and bring him here.

09:38.230 --> 09:39.980
She doesn't mean anything by it.

09:39.980 --> 09:41.800
She's not provoking him, either!

09:42.120 --> 09:43.750
All right.

09:43.750 --> 09:46.280
Let's take bets, guys!

09:46.280 --> 09:47.680
I bet they fail—

09:55.760 --> 09:58.300
50,000 dinah on the
Survivors pulling it off.

10:01.490 --> 10:02.820
And you?

10:03.670 --> 10:07.830
I... I bet my whole fortune
on the Survivors failing...

10:07.830 --> 10:09.220
Sorry!

10:09.220 --> 10:11.080
He's getting a little too heated.

10:11.930 --> 10:16.130
Go make some money while
you're waiting for us to get back.

10:16.780 --> 10:19.510
Okay, Ash, I bet on you!

10:19.510 --> 10:22.070
I bet tonight's bar tab on the lady!

10:22.070 --> 10:25.060
I bet my rent money that
the Survivors get killed!

10:28.010 --> 10:32.120
Garbage Collection. By far the
most dangerous slum in the city.

10:32.570 --> 10:35.620
They say there's no crime in the world
that hasn't happened here at least once.

10:35.620 --> 10:38.190
The Solar Knights don't come here, either.

10:38.770 --> 10:43.280
It was safe to assume that the guild
was right, and Hale was here.

10:46.820 --> 10:49.210
First, we say hello to the gatekeep.

10:49.950 --> 10:52.020
Ain't seen you around here before.

10:52.020 --> 10:53.880
Bounty hunters?

10:53.880 --> 10:55.750
Yeah, something like that.

10:55.750 --> 10:57.650
We don't need escorts or a guide.

10:58.180 --> 11:00.900
But I do want information.

11:01.400 --> 11:04.280
If it's about a bounty, go find it yourself.

11:04.280 --> 11:08.090
Has anything unusual happened around
here? Even something small.

11:08.970 --> 11:13.220
One of the whores got sick
and died last weekend.

11:13.220 --> 11:16.650
Greg, our odd-jobs guy,
had a dog that gave birth.

11:16.650 --> 11:19.600
Ten puppies. All males.

11:19.600 --> 11:21.180
Nobody's been dumb enough

11:21.180 --> 11:23.840
to let themselves get caught by a
bounty hunter for three months.

11:23.840 --> 11:28.610
Oh, and Greg says new
customers get 20 percent off.

11:28.610 --> 11:31.170
That doesn't tell us much.

11:31.490 --> 11:36.640
Guess I can throw in the fact that
a girl with a death wish came by.

11:36.640 --> 11:37.810
What?

11:38.360 --> 11:39.600
Thanks.

11:40.040 --> 11:44.290
If you die, make sure you die in a
way that keeps it out of the news.

11:46.360 --> 11:48.440
Oh, one more thing.

11:49.040 --> 11:52.310
Don't get in Nalgava's
way while he's working.

11:52.890 --> 11:54.570
That's a warning.

11:55.030 --> 11:56.530
Nalgava?

11:56.530 --> 11:58.070
Who's that?

11:58.340 --> 12:00.440
Someone important.

12:05.740 --> 12:06.790
It stinks.

12:07.480 --> 12:11.570
The air circulation and water quality
aren't very good, after all.

12:12.370 --> 12:16.710
There's all kinds of nasty
little maggots here...

12:19.000 --> 12:21.700
Hold it! This is a toll road.

12:21.700 --> 12:23.530
Hang over your money—

12:23.910 --> 12:25.850
We're looking for a man named Hale.

12:26.200 --> 12:29.470
Hale, the former host and seducer?

12:30.110 --> 12:31.950
He's in the Bedrooms.

12:31.950 --> 12:32.810
The Bedrooms?

12:34.250 --> 12:38.440
A building on the east side that
was supposed to be an inn.

12:35.540 --> 12:36.520
Schwing!

12:38.840 --> 12:40.080
Thanks.

12:41.840 --> 12:44.100
Then pay me for the info!

12:44.100 --> 12:46.750
You remember how you were just
trying to steal from us?

12:48.550 --> 12:51.170
You're going to die soon.

12:52.160 --> 12:54.000
You're doing something you shouldn't be.

12:54.000 --> 12:55.750
Nobody asked you.

12:58.570 --> 13:00.940
Does it make you feel happy? Depressed?

13:00.940 --> 13:02.770
What's your problem?

13:02.770 --> 13:04.540
Just answer the question.

13:05.440 --> 13:07.060
I can't sleep!

13:07.480 --> 13:10.580
I'm not allowed to have
some fun when I sleep?

13:10.580 --> 13:13.490
I can't live a normal life here!

13:13.490 --> 13:16.650
This wasn't supposed to be my life!

13:16.650 --> 13:18.820
You wouldn't understand!

13:18.820 --> 13:20.180
That's not true.

13:22.120 --> 13:23.630
That's not true.

13:25.110 --> 13:28.180
I understand. I think.

13:31.690 --> 13:34.040
This herb has calming properties.

13:34.360 --> 13:36.360
This can be your fee for that information.

13:37.210 --> 13:40.360
It's not a strong medicine,
but it will have to do.

13:40.760 --> 13:43.320
Don't rely on what you've
been taking until now.

13:44.920 --> 13:46.340
W-Wait!

13:47.360 --> 13:49.560
Hale's a fast runner.

13:49.560 --> 13:51.620
If he sees you coming, he'll be
gone in the blink of an eye.

13:52.490 --> 13:54.920
Thanks. We'll be careful.

13:57.060 --> 13:59.610
So this is the Bedrooms.

13:59.610 --> 14:02.850
If Hale gets even the slightest
bit suspicious, he'll bolt.

14:02.850 --> 14:04.520
We'll have to be careful.

14:16.110 --> 14:17.380
You okay?

14:19.780 --> 14:20.710
I'm sorry.

14:20.710 --> 14:24.850
The conditions here are so bad,
it's no wonder people are getting sick.

14:25.500 --> 14:27.680
There's no hope.

14:28.100 --> 14:32.330
If anything, this is where
you'd need a temple...

14:35.540 --> 14:36.480
Find him?

14:36.820 --> 14:40.300
Yeah, he's here...

14:40.300 --> 14:42.480
What? That doesn't tell me much.

14:43.030 --> 14:45.060
He's busy, from the look of it.

14:48.280 --> 14:50.110
Wh-Who the hell are you?

14:50.410 --> 14:52.950
Most people with a bounty on their
head are a little more careful.

14:52.950 --> 14:54.950
Stay out!

14:54.950 --> 14:56.870
An easy 300,000!

14:57.110 --> 14:59.770
What do you mean, 300,000?

14:59.770 --> 15:01.260
The bounty on you.

15:01.260 --> 15:03.870
That's way too much money!

15:04.160 --> 15:07.800
I just hit, kicked, sold into
slavery, and conned people!

15:07.800 --> 15:09.010
And murder?

15:09.010 --> 15:10.590
I didn't do it!

15:15.540 --> 15:18.170
Well, you can tell the guild all about it.

15:19.560 --> 15:20.770
You.

15:21.080 --> 15:23.170
What are you doing to my patient?

15:23.170 --> 15:24.390
Dr. Nalgava!

15:24.390 --> 15:26.070
Help me!

15:26.570 --> 15:27.920
Nalgava?

15:29.280 --> 15:30.870
That's him?

15:32.950 --> 15:34.580
Who are you?

15:34.580 --> 15:36.690
You don't look like amateurs.

15:36.690 --> 15:37.790
And you?

15:37.790 --> 15:40.250
You don't look like the usual priest.

15:41.440 --> 15:43.670
The Bedrooms are a neutral zone.

15:43.670 --> 15:46.910
The deal says you don't interfere
when I'm treating patients.

15:46.910 --> 15:50.120
Wait. We're not from here.

15:50.120 --> 15:51.920
We just came to capture a bounty.

15:54.000 --> 15:55.790
What did Hale do?

15:55.790 --> 15:58.640
Most everything except murder.

15:58.640 --> 15:59.970
What?

16:00.590 --> 16:02.310
Fool.

16:02.590 --> 16:07.190
I can cure wounds and disease,
but I can't remove your guilt.

16:07.190 --> 16:11.220
If he's done evil, then I
have no reason to stop you.

16:11.650 --> 16:12.880
Take him.

16:12.880 --> 16:15.700
No, Doctor! Do something!

16:16.780 --> 16:18.570
He has the Yellow Demon Sickness.

16:19.580 --> 16:22.100
If he's not coming back for a long time,

16:22.100 --> 16:24.690
I'd like to at least treat
him before he goes.

16:24.690 --> 16:26.310
You're sure?

16:26.310 --> 16:30.160
If we take him, your treatment
might go to waste.

16:31.360 --> 16:33.120
Kid, that's...

16:32.440 --> 16:34.840
Nick, that's incorrect.

16:36.310 --> 16:39.070
Depending on what he's done,
he may get the death penalty.

16:39.070 --> 16:40.840
Hey! Don't even say that!

16:40.840 --> 16:45.960
But our job is to do the best
we can at any given moment.

16:46.630 --> 16:51.860
It may even turn out that he didn't
do anything he's accused of.

16:51.860 --> 16:54.300
And it's also possible he
may lead a peaceful life,

16:54.300 --> 16:56.600
and die a peaceful death, in prison.

16:56.600 --> 16:59.760
Quiet! Shut up and take
away me already, asshole!

16:59.760 --> 17:01.840
You're a priest, then?

17:01.840 --> 17:06.200
Yes. Former priest, just like you, though...

17:07.280 --> 17:10.990
If I may ask, why are you here?

17:10.990 --> 17:13.830
If you're talented enough to
identify Yellow Demon Sickness,

17:13.830 --> 17:15.790
you could work anywhere you like.

17:16.300 --> 17:19.270
Then what about you?

17:19.270 --> 17:21.770
Do you want to go back to being a priest?

17:21.770 --> 17:22.580
Yes.

17:23.420 --> 17:25.310
I'm sick of it all.

17:27.300 --> 17:29.400
By the way, Nalgava.

17:30.490 --> 17:31.890
Stepping Man.

17:33.020 --> 17:35.260
Have you heard of him?

17:35.260 --> 17:38.040
Of course he hasn't!

17:38.040 --> 17:41.750
A black shadow that stalks in the
night and kidnaps children...

17:43.210 --> 17:46.170
I'm afraid I haven't.

17:47.450 --> 17:51.510
A kidnapper? This place is filled with 'em!

17:51.510 --> 17:53.780
Who cares about one kidnapper?

17:53.780 --> 17:56.780
Hey. He seems genuinely concerned.

17:56.780 --> 17:58.210
If you know something...

17:58.210 --> 17:58.920
Oh!

17:59.280 --> 18:02.580
Well, I don't know if they're a kidnapper,

18:02.580 --> 18:06.900
but I did see this weird reporter going
around and giving kids candy to talk to them.

18:06.900 --> 18:08.430
Weird reporter?

18:09.660 --> 18:10.860
You pulled it off.

18:11.320 --> 18:14.100
You found him in a single day. Nice.

18:14.100 --> 18:15.730
I-I can't believe it!

18:16.140 --> 18:18.380
They really found him!

18:19.110 --> 18:22.870
Now, how much did you all bet?

18:24.600 --> 18:26.360
Right now, I've got about 800,000 dinah...

18:26.360 --> 18:27.240
That'll do.

18:28.160 --> 18:29.630
W-Wait!

18:29.630 --> 18:32.240
Some of that goes to the ones who
bet on you! You can't take it all!

18:33.180 --> 18:36.000
Use this money to buy every
bottle of alcohol you can find!

18:36.770 --> 18:38.310
Drinks on the house for everyone!

18:40.570 --> 18:43.150
Nice thinking, missy!

18:43.780 --> 18:46.520
Hey, I bet on you!

18:46.520 --> 18:48.930
You were gonna blow it on booze anyway!

18:48.930 --> 18:51.640
Or are you too good to
drink what I offer you?

18:51.640 --> 18:53.830
She's got you there!

18:53.830 --> 18:55.770
Oh, fine.

18:58.220 --> 18:59.450
Sorry...

19:02.910 --> 19:05.420
Ow...

19:05.900 --> 19:08.380
Thanks for the booze last night.

19:09.400 --> 19:11.570
Here's the money for Hale, and...

19:11.570 --> 19:14.070
you wanted the stuff on Stepping Man, right?

19:14.650 --> 19:16.290
Let's see...

19:16.540 --> 19:20.420
"Burn green wood in your house and
the smoke will keep him away."

19:20.690 --> 19:25.890
"He knocked a hole in my roof,
but fixed my gutters. Nice guy."

19:25.890 --> 19:30.240
"I stayed up late at night to summon him,
and he told me to go to bed.

19:30.240 --> 19:31.410
I'm sorry."

19:32.560 --> 19:35.570
Nothing but weird rumors
and mistaken identity.

19:35.930 --> 19:39.680
Personally, I'd rather you
went after normal bounties

19:39.680 --> 19:42.360
instead of chasing non-existent folklore.

19:42.360 --> 19:43.850
Ow...

19:43.850 --> 19:47.590
We're not interested in
Stepping Man the urban legend, either.

19:47.970 --> 19:51.990
We want to find the kidnapper
that people call Stepping Man.

19:53.120 --> 19:55.840
I don't know about kidnappers...

19:56.160 --> 19:58.730
But if you're looking for a suspicious
person who talks to kids,

19:58.730 --> 20:00.010
you can find her over there.

20:02.390 --> 20:05.120
A weird reporter going around
and giving kids candy...

20:05.120 --> 20:07.690
...to talk to them?

20:09.570 --> 20:11.230
No way.

20:11.230 --> 20:16.220
She's definitely the reporter
giving kids candy, but...

20:16.460 --> 20:19.980
If only you remembered more
about what they looked like...

20:20.280 --> 20:25.210
I just remember that they were fast
on their feet, and used chains...

20:25.210 --> 20:26.170
Chains?

20:28.780 --> 20:31.870
She was weirdly heavy.

20:32.280 --> 20:35.120
If she had chains wrapped around her body...

20:35.120 --> 20:36.450
That's silly.

20:37.610 --> 20:39.350
No way!

20:41.200 --> 20:45.030
Curran, Tiana. Block the exits.

20:45.980 --> 20:48.200
I'm sure I'm being overly cautious, but...

20:48.200 --> 20:49.910
Oh, Nick!

20:49.910 --> 20:52.390
She found us on our way back
to visit Reina's mom...

20:52.390 --> 20:57.200
So you give the kids candy and
interview them, and then what?

20:57.490 --> 20:59.140
Then what?

20:59.140 --> 21:02.080
Oh, my! You look angry!

21:02.080 --> 21:05.650
I don't know if being a reporter
is a busy job or not.

21:06.060 --> 21:08.740
One minute you're sitting around waiting,

21:08.740 --> 21:11.340
and the next you're leaping around the city!

21:11.340 --> 21:12.830
And from roof to roof?

21:14.280 --> 21:18.190
For example, where were you two nights ago?

21:18.190 --> 21:18.830
Huh?

21:19.110 --> 21:21.640
Is this turning into an interrogation?

21:21.640 --> 21:22.840
You can't answer?

21:23.470 --> 21:24.740
I can!

21:24.740 --> 21:27.100
Editing department! Bar!
Turned in assignment! Ate!

21:27.100 --> 21:28.270
Article! Food!

21:28.270 --> 21:30.570
Kinda sucked! Was pretty good!

21:30.570 --> 21:34.960
Well, I may have explained
them out of order,

21:34.960 --> 21:38.110
thus making two simple to understand events

21:38.110 --> 21:40.110
difficult to understand by
discussing them in parallel.

21:40.110 --> 21:44.300
This is a sign of my powerful
literary skills...

21:41.120 --> 21:43.920
So, are you Stepping Man?

21:45.740 --> 21:48.110
Where'd you take the kids?

21:48.370 --> 21:50.110
Why do you kidnap them?

21:50.110 --> 21:53.860
No, who even are you?

21:54.520 --> 21:59.750
Um... I'm not sure I understand
what you're asking.

22:14.080 --> 22:15.350
Seriously?

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
Next time:
"Labyrinth Dragnet"

23:36.560 --> 23:39.290
Next time: "Labyrinth Dragnet".
